file_merger: inference uses the casting rules to type a value (checkpoint 1)

Sentence: the schema-inference bullets under "If --schema not provided", next to "Type
priority: timestamp > date > bool > int > float > string". The strict-driver run of
min12-ABDJKMN on v1 (registry T3, Risk 35) quoted both the priority list and the casting
rule "`bool` includes `1`/`0` along with standard values" and still read the `1`/`0`
allowance as governing casting into a declared bool column only, so a `1` and a `true` across
two files conflicted and the column fell to string. The hidden test cross_family_coercion
expects `bool`, and the reference solution's detector applies the same parsers inference and
casting share, bool first. The added line ties inference to the casting rules instead of
restating the bool case. Test: spec_correct/cross_family_coercion (checkpoint 1).

